  "description": "The Animal Justice Party merges its emphasis on animal welfare with concerns regarding the climate, sustainability and equality. Founded in 2023, Auckland-based candidate Robert McNeil, who co-leads the party alongside Danette Wereta, cited both a lack of Green party candidates standing in East Auckland seats and a perception that the Greens have to compromise as the genesis for the party. In 2023, it received 0.17% percent, or 5,018 votes, but it has never won a seat in Parliament. ",
